# ComposeUX HTML/DOM render backend — form/control layer as native DOM, browser-as-live-peer control->publish; PLACEMENT UNRATIFIED [SPEC:CXC-DOM]

> v1 renders the form/control/layout subset of a `.compose.yaml` scene as NATIVE DOM elements —
> leveraging HTML for free accessibility, keyboard nav, and i18n, never redrawing an `<input>` or a
> `<button>` as raster pixels on an HTML5 canvas. Rich graphics (gauges, data viz, the colonial UX) are
> a SEPARATE, DEFERRED backend for the WEB — CanvasKit (Skia compiled to WASM), David-ruled 2026-08-25
> pending the render-engineer's live-doc verification; MOBILE IS DEFERRED ENTIRELY, no RN-Skia
> commitment. React Native Skia forks the imperative Canvas contract into a React paradigm and is NOT
> the base graphics library, but it remains a legitimate PER-WIDGET escape hatch for a widget that is
> inherently platform-bound ([DX-REALIZATION-DECLARES-ENVELOPE]) — never the default. A page composes
> both: DOM chrome around canvas islands. The
> control->publish contract already exists natively (`emit_button`/`text_input`/`radio_button_group`
> publish via `RenderContext.publish()`); this backend RE-REALIZES it in the browser over the WS
> connector ([SPEC:CXC-WS]), adds a NEW form-buffered-atomic-submit publish mode alongside the existing
> live-publish one, and validates config submissions SERVER-SIDE by reusing the ComposeServer plugin
> loader's real pydantic evaluator ([CXC-CSL-CONFIG-VALIDATION]) — never a client-side JS
> reimplementation of validation logic that could drift from what actually runs. Reuse-by-reference:
> the `Canvas` 30-ish-method ABC (canvas.py, measured 35 abstract + 2 concrete-default), the
> `.compose.yaml` scene format, the binding-DSL grammar, the control-publish vocabulary. Reimplement:
> the browser JS runtime — the third reactive tier after Python/Skia and C++/CYD — conformance-matched
> to the Python golden reference exactly as CYD/Skia parity already is.

---

