## 16. Error and boundary matrix

### [CXC-DOM-BOUNDARIES] Every condition a builder would otherwise have to invent an answer for

| # | Condition | Required behaviour |
|---|-----------|--------------------|
| 1 | A widget type has no entry in the control renderer registry AND is not a plain layout/chrome primitive | falls through to the generic `Canvas`-primitive path if it draws via Canvas calls at all; if it is a genuinely unsupported type (e.g. a graphics widget on a DOM-only build), rendered as a NAMED placeholder, never silently blank ([CXC-DOM-HYBRID-COMPOSITION]) |
| 2 | A control inside a form fires its change event | writes to the form's local buffer only; ZERO bus traffic ([CXC-DOM-PUBLISH-MODES]) |
| 3 | A form is submitted with one or more invalid fields | ZERO bus publishes for the whole form; per-field `config:<field>` errors returned and displayed; all edited (including valid) field values remain in the buffer, unpublished and unreverted ([CXC-DOM-FORM-PRIMITIVE]) |
| 4 | A form is abandoned (unmounted) without submitting | ZERO bus publishes for any buffered field; the edit is discarded, never auto-committed ([CXC-DOM-FORM-PRIMITIVE]) |
| 5 | A bus-side update arrives for a namespace bound by a field CURRENTLY being edited in an open form | the buffer/display is NOT overwritten by the incoming value — the user's uncommitted edit wins until submit or cancel ([CXC-DOM-TWO-WAY-BINDING]) |
| 6 | The SAME bus-side update arrives for a namespace bound by a LIVE (non-form) control | the control's display updates immediately, within one frame ([CXC-DOM-TWO-WAY-BINDING]) |
| 7 | A control publishes a value it just received as its own bound value (echo) | suppressed once, mirroring `TextInputWidget`'s existing echo-suppression precedent — never a publish/re-apply feedback loop ([CXC-DOM-TWO-WAY-BINDING]) |
| 8 | A pydantic `Config` field's type has no v1 control mapping (e.g. `list[SomeModel]`) | falls back to the ratified raw-mode DSL path ([CXC-CS-RULE-CONFIG-UX]); this backend never attempts a partial/broken structured editor for it ([CXC-DOM-CONTROL-SET-V1]) |
| 9 | Client-side presentation hints (a browser-native min/max) would have accepted a value the server rejects | server rejection is unconditional and authoritative regardless of what the client hint allowed through ([CXC-DOM-SERVER-VALIDATION]) |
| 10 | A widget type is fully served by DOM (control registry or primitive path) | its CanvasKit/Skia-in-browser realization is never built, loaded, or referenced — the laziness is structural, not merely deferred profiling ([CXC-DOM-REALIZATION-SPLIT]) |
| 11 | A scene nests a form widget inside another form widget | loud parse/mount-time error naming the offending widget id; v1 does not support nested forms ([CXC-DOM-FORM-PRIMITIVE]) |
| 12 | The WS connection this backend rides on is not yet `BOUND` (per [CXC-WS-LIFECYCLE]) | no control publish and no binding subscription is attempted before `BOUND`; this backend inherits [CXC-WS-BOUNDARIES] condition 3 unchanged |

- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-DOM]

---

## 17. Acceptance — machine signal + glass gate

### [CXC-DOM-ACCEPTANCE] The backend's two-tier verdict — a machine signal AND, for every failure class human eyes can catch that a narrow test cannot, an explicit human/glass gate

- definition: per [DX-SPEC-CARRIES-ITS-EVIDENCE] and the loader/WS-spec precedent
  ([CXC-CSL-ACCEPTANCE], [CXC-WS-ACCEPTANCE]), machine-green alone never accepts this backend — the
  failure classes that matter most here (an inaccessible control that passes a naive click test, a
  buffered edit silently reaching the bus, a validation error that displays on the wrong field) are
  exactly the ones a narrow unit test can pass while the real browser experience is broken.
  [CXC-VISION-EPISTEMICS] applies throughout this table.

| ID | Requirement | verify-machine | verify-human (glass) |
|----|-------------|-----------------|------------------------|
| DOM-V1 | Controls realize as native DOM elements, never redrawn on raster canvas ([CXC-DOM-SCOPE-SPLIT]) | axe-core audit reports zero name/role/value violations on v1 controls | screen-reader pass (VoiceOver/NVDA) operates every control without a mouse |
| DOM-V2 | Rich graphics stay out of this backend entirely ([CXC-DOM-SCOPE-SPLIT]) | zero CanvasKit/WASM references in a control-only scene's network trace | n/a — structural |
| DOM-V3 | Hybrid composition — DOM chrome + canvas islands coexist without coordination ([CXC-DOM-HYBRID-COMPOSITION]) | mixed-scene fixture renders both independently; DOM-only fixture has zero graphics-backend requests | a real mixed page (once CanvasKit exists) shows both realized correctly side by side |
| DOM-V4 | Control renderer registry dispatch is correct and canvas realization stays lazy ([CXC-DOM-REALIZATION-SPLIT]) | registry dispatch spy-asserted per widget type; zero CanvasKit calls for a control-only scene | none required |
| DOM-V5 | DOM `Canvas` subclass implements the full ABC with correct stack semantics ([CXC-DOM-CANVAS-SUBCLASS]) | golden-fixture primitive sequence matches the element-map table; save/restore/clip stress test passes | side-by-side visual comparison against Skia/SVG renders of the same fixture |
| DOM-V6 | Re-realized controls publish the SAME payload shape as their Python originals ([CXC-DOM-CONTROL-PUBLISH-REUSE]) | scripted DOM interaction's outbound WS frame matches the equivalent headless Python widget test | real click observed by a live subscriber on the same bus |
| DOM-V7 | Publish mode selected correctly by form-container membership ([CXC-DOM-PUBLISH-MODES]) | identical control inside/outside a form produces buffered-vs-immediate publish correctly | none required beyond DOM-V9's glass gate |
| DOM-V8 | Form buffers, validates, and publishes atomically ([CXC-DOM-FORM-PRIMITIVE]) | unsubmitted edits produce zero publishes; valid submit produces one atomic sequence; invalid submit produces zero publishes plus per-field errors, buffer retained | a real form fill-submit-see-it-take-effect (or see-the-specific-error) end to end |
| DOM-V9 | Validation is server-side, reusing the loader's real evaluator ([CXC-DOM-SERVER-VALIDATION]) | a value only a cross-field/non-DOM-expressible constraint rejects is still rejected server-side | operator submits a deliberately invalid config and reads a specific, named field error |
| DOM-V10 | Two-way binding: display tracks bus outside a form, buffer wins inside one ([CXC-DOM-TWO-WAY-BINDING]) | scripted bus publish updates the live control, not the mid-edit form field, within one frame | two-tab scenario: live tab updates instantly, editing tab is undisturbed until submit |
| DOM-V11 | v1 control vocabulary is exactly the named set; editable collections correctly fall back to raw-mode ([CXC-DOM-CONTROL-SET-V1]) | fixture schema covering every v1 type renders correctly; a `list[Model]` field falls back to raw-mode, never a broken structured editor | David/render-engineer review of a real generated config form |
| DOM-V12 | Rides the WS connector; SSE bridge stays read-only, unextended ([CXC-DOM-TRANSPORT]) | source scan finds no `EventSource`/SSE-write reference in this backend | none required beyond [CXC-WS-ACCEPTANCE]'s own gates |
| DOM-V13 | JS runtime conformance-matches the Python golden reference ([CXC-DOM-REUSE-REIMPLEMENT-RUNTIME]) | shared `dsl_corpus.json` conformance corpus passes identically against Python and JS evaluators (measured 234/234 bit-exact IEEE-754, [DD-DOM-DSL-EVAL-REUSE]); cross-tier scene-parse parity fixture passes | none required — fully machine-observable via the conformance corpus |
| DOM-V14 | Placement recorded, not silent ([CXC-DOM-PLACEMENT]) | the spec carries the `[PLACEMENT UNRATIFIED]` node + the filename-check property | n/a — structural |

- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-DOM]
- see-also: [DX-SPEC-CARRIES-ITS-EVIDENCE], [CXC-VISION-EPISTEMICS], [CXC-CSL-ACCEPTANCE], [CXC-WS-ACCEPTANCE]

---

## 18. Evidence — pre-integration questions answered, post-integration slots EMPTY until a real build

### [CXC-DOM-EVIDENCE] Pre-integration questions (answered by this design pass) and post-integration evidence (EMPTY — never run)

- pre-integration questions answered by this spec: (1) DOM vs. redraw-in-canvas for controls -> native
  DOM elements, never redrawn, [CXC-DOM-SCOPE-SPLIT]; (2) rich-graphics backend choice -> CanvasKit, not
  RN-Skia, deferred, [CXC-DOM-SCOPE-SPLIT]; (3) composition of the two backends -> hybrid, per-widget-
  class dispatch, canvas realization built lazily, [CXC-DOM-HYBRID-COMPOSITION]/[CXC-DOM-REALIZATION-SPLIT];
  (4) the fallback layout/chrome realization -> a generic `Canvas` ABC subclass with an explicit style/
  transform stack, [CXC-DOM-CANVAS-SUBCLASS]; (5) control->publish contract -> reused, re-realized per
  widget type, [CXC-DOM-CONTROL-PUBLISH-REUSE]; (6) publish-mode selection -> structural, by form-
  container membership, [CXC-DOM-PUBLISH-MODES]; (7) the form primitive's shape -> buffer/validate-on-
  submit/atomic-publish, generalizing `text_input`'s commit model, [CXC-DOM-FORM-PRIMITIVE]; (8)
  validation authority -> server-side, reusing [CXC-CSL-CONFIG-VALIDATION], no client-side reimpl,
  [CXC-DOM-SERVER-VALIDATION]; (9) two-way binding precedence during an in-progress form edit -> the
  buffer wins over a concurrent bus update, [CXC-DOM-TWO-WAY-BINDING]; (10) v1 control vocabulary ->
  the eight named field types, editable collections deferred, [CXC-DOM-CONTROL-SET-V1]; (11) the config-
  UI generator's relationship to this spec -> consumer, not part of it, [CXC-DOM-CONFIG-UI-CONSUMER];
  (12) reuse/reimplement boundary -> contract reused by reference, runtime reimplemented in JS,
  conformance-matched, [CXC-DOM-REUSE-REIMPLEMENT-RUNTIME]; (13) transport -> the WS connector, SSE
  stays legacy read-only, [CXC-DOM-TRANSPORT].
- pre-integration questions LEFT open, flagged for render-engineer/David ratify (not silently resolved):
  the editable nested-collection control design, deliberately deferred
  ([DD-DOM-EDITABLE-COLLECTIONS]); tree virtualization/windowing at scale, noted but not a v1 blocker
  ([DD-DOM-TREE-VIRTUALIZATION]). CORRECTED 2026-08-25 (diamond-remediation): the DSL evaluator's exact
  reuse mechanism ([DD-DOM-DSL-EVAL-REUSE]) is NO LONGER open — it is RESOLVED by implementation
  (candidate (b), the corpus-gated independent JS evaluator, measured 234/234); moved out of this list.
- evidence-dom-canvas-subclass: EMPTY — no DOM `Canvas` subclass exists in this repository as of this
  spec's authoring (2026-08-25); this is a build spec, not a report of landed code.
- evidence-control-registry-real-browser: EMPTY — no real browser has rendered a v1 control set from
  this backend (DOM-V1/DOM-V5/DOM-V11's human gates unrun).
- evidence-form-real-submit: EMPTY — no real form submission has round-tripped through server-side
  validation over a real WS connection (DOM-V8/DOM-V9's human gates unrun).
- evidence-two-tab-binding: EMPTY — no real two-tab scenario has confirmed DOM-V10's live-vs-buffered
  precedence.
- evidence-js-conformance-corpus: FILLED (diamond-remediation, 2026-08-25) — the shared `dsl_corpus.json`
  conformance corpus HAS been run against the JS evaluator: 234/234 bit-exact IEEE-754 against the
  Python golden reference, per [DD-DOM-DSL-EVAL-REUSE]'s resolution. DOM-V13's machine gate is
  exercised. This is the ONE evidence slot in this table no longer EMPTY; every other slot below remains
  EMPTY exactly as authored — this correction does not claim the rest of the backend has been built.
- evidence-accessibility-audit: EMPTY — no axe-core or screen-reader pass has been run against a real
  rendered scene (DOM-V1's gates unrun).
- why-empty-matters: per [DX-SPEC-CARRIES-ITS-EVIDENCE], "never run at all" must be a QUERYABLE
  PROPERTY, not something a reader has to already know — every slot above is `EMPTY` explicitly rather
  than simply absent, so a future query against this node can distinguish "not yet built" from "nobody
  thought to record it."
- status: draft
- status-detail: draft — every evidence slot EMPTY by construction; this spec has not been implemented
- provenance: architect-synthesis
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-DOM]
- see-also: [DX-SPEC-CARRIES-ITS-EVIDENCE], [CXC-DOM-ACCEPTANCE]

