**Version**: 0.3 — 2026-08-25, diamond-remediation revision, per the WS<->DOM integration's completed
diamond findings. (1) [DD-DOM-DSL-EVAL-REUSE] is RESOLVED, not open: candidate (b), an independent
hand-written JS evaluator gated by the shared `dsl_corpus.json` conformance corpus (also consumed by the
CH32/CYD tier) — measured 234/234 bit-exact IEEE-754 against the Python golden reference, satisfying
[CXC-DOM-REUSE-REIMPLEMENT-RUNTIME]'s one-measurement-path constraint per the gap-analyzer's own
endorsement. Provenance: architect-synthesis (the render-engineer's call under the fixed constraint),
not a further David ratify. DOM-V13's acceptance row and `evidence-js-conformance-corpus` are updated to
match — the ONE evidence slot in [CXC-DOM-EVIDENCE] no longer EMPTY. (2) [CXC-DOM-SERVER-VALIDATION]
gains a `loader-landed-reuse-tightened` note: [SPEC:CXC-CS-LOADER] has LANDED (`42d3285`,
`composeserver_loader.py`), so this node's "reuse [CXC-CSL-CONFIG-VALIDATION]" is no longer a forward
reference — the WS<->DOM integration is wiring it through a SHARED `validate_config(cls, payload)`
function BOTH the loader and this backend's `validation.py` import, closing the second-independent-
validation-path gap the gap-analyzer flagged as finding P1. This SUPERSEDES the v0.2 footer's claim that
[CXC-DOM-SERVER-VALIDATION] "audited clean and are UNCHANGED" — it is changed by this revision, in
substance (import-the-shared-function) not in its original MUST/MUST NOT requirements, which remain
david-ruling and untouched. Previously version 0.2 — 2026-08-25, revised per the independent provenance audit
(`docs/composeserver/AUDIT-dom-backend.md`) and David's resulting rulings
([DEC-DOM-AUDIT-RESOLVED-2026-08-25]). Q1 (was CanvasKit ratified, or still pending?): David ruled
CanvasKit for the deferred WEB rich-graphics path, MOBILE DEFERRED ENTIRELY, and restored the
architect's original "pending render-engineer live-doc verification" caveat this spec had dropped
([CXC-DOM-SCOPE-SPLIT]). Q2 (read-only or editable v1 table?): David confirmed READ-ONLY table (not
just tree) is the correct v1 line, editable deferred to the raw-mode fallback
