[CXC-DOM-SCOPE-SPLIT] is now explicitly three-way (the scope split = david-ruling; the
CanvasKit-for-web/mobile-deferred-entirely selection = ALSO david-ruling, David's own 2026-08-25 call;
the RN-Skia-as-escape-hatch framing = architect-recommendation); [DD-DOM-TREE-VIRTUALIZATION] re-tagged
`david-ruling` -> `architect-synthesis` (David never mentioned virtualization/windowing — that was the
architect's own parenthetical); [CXC-DOM-CONTROL-SET-V1] and the five Fork-B mechanic nodes
([CXC-DOM-CONTROL-PUBLISH-REUSE], [CXC-DOM-PUBLISH-MODES], [CXC-DOM-FORM-PRIMITIVE],
[CXC-DOM-TWO-WAY-BINDING], [CXC-DOM-CONFIG-UI-CONSUMER]) re-tagged `david-ruling` ->
`david-ratified-by-concurrence`, citing the blanket "I concur, proceed" (line 26423) rather than
implying six separate David rulings. [CXC-DOM-SERVER-VALIDATION] (the one Fork-B node with genuine
([CXC-DOM-REUSE-REIMPLEMENT-RUNTIME], honestly `architect-synthesis` throughout) audited clean and are
UNCHANGED. v0.1 was the initial build spec, authored from the composeio-hardware-architect's design
